-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Left Front Contraction
-- statement:
--   **The left-front switcheroo aggregate is a contraction.**
--
--   Fix a slice-pair question $q=(x,y)$. For a polynomial outcome $g$ of the slice family at $x$ and an outcome $o$ of the projective submeasurement at $y$, write $G^x_g$ and $M^y_o$ for their operators. The family of left-placed products is
--
--   $$
--   A_{g,o}=(G^x_gM^y_o)\otimes I.
--   $$
--
--   Its adjoint-square sum is bounded by the identity:
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{g,o}A_{g,o}^{\dagger}A_{g,o}\le I.
--   $$
--
--   The proof uses that the polynomial outcomes are projections, that the complete-part total operator is bounded by the identity, and that a projective submeasurement sandwiches every positive contraction by a sum bounded by the identity. This contraction is the witness for the final square-root estimate in the left-front switcheroo comparison.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateLeftFront_contraction`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
